# Summary
Introduced: streaming routing now accepts PUT/UploadPart without x-amz-content-sha256 and authenticates using an empty-body hash, so the payload is no longer covered by SigV4 for such requests.
The commit changes routing so all PUT/UploadPart requests (except copy-source) use the streaming path, regardless of whether x-amz-content-sha256 is present. For requests missing this header, parse_chunked_mode returns ChunkedMode::None and the streaming handler builds an S3Request from headers only. Authentication then uses a SHA-256 of the empty body, and no later payload hash check occurs because no hash was claimed. This allows a signed request to be accepted even though the signature is not bound to the actual payload, enabling body tampering or unsigned uploads when the content hash header is omitted.

