## Report
Attempted dynamic validation: `cargo build -p argmin-s3` failed because `ec-sys` requires libisal (build.rs panic: missing libisal.pc), so no runnable binary; `valgrind` and `gdb` are not installed in the environment. Code review shows: (1) all PUT/UploadPart requests without x-amz-copy-source are routed into the streaming path via `is_streaming_write` regardless of x-amz-content-sha256, and missing header yields `ChunkedMode::None` (crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:287-402). (2) Streaming handlers build `S3Request` from headers only (`from_hyper_headers`), so body is empty (crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:486-489). `body_hash` falls back to sha256 of `req.body` when x-amz-content-sha256 is missing (crates/server-http/src/http/request.rs:75-104). Authentication computes body_hash from header or sha256(body) when header missing (crates/auth/src/request.rs:114-119); thus in streaming path it uses the empty-body hash. (3) Streaming prepare uses `authenticate_with_payload_check(req, false)` (crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs:1750-1757), so no payload hash recheck. The streaming loop only verifies payload hash when a fixed `x-amz-content-sha256` is supplied; `claimed_payload_sha256_from_parts` returns None when the header is absent and the mismatch check is skipped (crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs:635-643, 1165-1176). Therefore a client can sign an empty payload and omit x-amz-content-sha256, yet send a non-empty body that is accepted, matching the reported vulnerability.

